...)` — it is a plain struct field\n\nIt therefore does not meet either condition: the accessed storage is **not associated** with the calling `AtomWallet`. Accessing it from within `validateUserOp` violates `STO-021`/`STO-022`. A compliant bundler simulating the UserOp detects the non-associated external storage read and **rejects the UserOp**. This is not a configuration issue — it is a fundamental incompatibility between the `owner()` implementation and the ERC-7562 storage access rules.\n\n### Scope of Impact\n\nEvery `AtomWallet` begins life unclaimed (`isClaimed == false`), with `ATOM_WARDEN` as its effective owner via the dynamic `owner()` lookup. The wallet can only be claimed once the user calls `acceptOwnership()` after a two-step transfer. Until that happens:\n\n- Every UserOp submitted for the wallet will be **rejected at simulation** by any ERC-7562-compliant bundler (e.g., Pimlico, Alchemy, Biconomy, Stackup, the canonical eth-infinitism bundler).\n- The wallet cannot be used as an ERC-4337 smart account until claimed.\n- The `ATOM_WARDEN` — the party responsible for acting on behalf of unclaimed atoms — is also blocked from submitting UserOps on those atoms via standard bundling infrastructure.\n\nGiven that unclaimed wallets are the initial state for **all** atoms created in the system, this effectively disables ERC-4337 functionality for every newly created atom.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nCache the `atomWarden` address in contract storage at initialization time so that `owner()` reads only from the wallet's own storage during validation:\n\n```diff\n+   address private _atomWarden;  // cached at initialization\n\n    function initialize(\n        IEntryPoint _entryPoint,\n        address _multiVault,\n        bytes32 _atomId\n    ) external initializer {\n        ...\n+       _atomWarden = IMultiVault(_multiVault).getAtomWarden();\n-       __Ownable_init(IMultiVault(_multiVault).getAtomWarden());\n+       __Ownable_init(_atomWarden);\n        ...\n    }\n\n    function owner() public view override returns (address) {\n        OwnableStorage storage $ = _getAtomWalletOwnerStorage();\n-       return isClaimed ? $._owner : multiVault.getAtomWarden();\n+       return isClaimed ? $._owner : _atomWarden;\n    }\n```\n\nWith this change, `owner()` reads from the wallet's own associated storage in both the claimed and unclaimed states, satisfying ERC-7562 validation-phase restrictions. If the protocol requires the warden address to be updatable after deployment, a separate `updateAtomWarden()` function callable only outside the validation phase can sync the cached value.",
      "proofOfConcept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nAdd the following test inside `tests/PoCCore.t.sol`.\n\n```solidity\nimport { PackedUserOperation } from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/PackedUserOperation.sol\";\nimport { AtomWallet } from \"src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol\";\n```\n\n```solidity\n    function test_2unclaimedAtomWalletValidateUserOpCallsMultiVaultExternally() external {\n    \n    \n        uint256 atomCost = protocol.multiVault.getAtomCost();\n        bytes[] memory atomData = new bytes[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        atomData[0] = abi.encodePacked(\"poc8-atom\");\n        amounts[0] = atomCost;\n\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        bytes32[] memory atomIds = protocol.multiVault.createAtoms{ value: atomCost }(atomData, amounts);\n        bytes32 atomId = atomIds[0];\n\n        address walletAddr = protocol.atomWalletFactory.deployAtomWallet(atomId);\n        AtomWallet wallet = AtomWallet(payable(walletAddr));\n\n        \n        assertFalse(wallet.isClaimed(), \"wallet must be unclaimed for ERC-7562 violation to manifest\");\n\n        \n        // Produce a valid 65-byte ECDSA signature so that ECDSA.tryRecover returns NoError\n        // and execution reaches `recovered != owner()` at line 309, triggering the external\n        // call to multiVault.  Private key 1 signs the Ethereum-prefixed userOpHash.\n\n        bytes32 userOpHash = keccak256(\"poc8-userop-hash\");\n        bytes32 ethSignedHash =\n            keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", userOpHash));\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(1, ethSignedHash);\n        bytes memory sig = abi.encodePacked(r, s, v); // 65 bytes\n\n        PackedUserOperation memory userOp;\n        userOp.sender    = walletAddr;\n        userOp.signature = sig;\n\n        // vm.expectCall verifies that multiVault.getAtomWarden() is called at least once\n        // during the validateUserOp execution below.  This proves the external call occurs\n        // during the ERC-4337 validation phase, violating ERC-7562.\n        vm.expectCall(\n            address(protocol.multiVault),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(bytes4(keccak256(\"getAtomWarden()\")))\n        );\n        \n        console2.log(\"AtomWallet address :\", walletAddr);\n        console2.log(\"isClaimed          :\", wallet.isClaimed());\n        console2.log(\"multiVault address :\", address(protocol.multiVault));\n        console2.log(\"---\");\n        console2.log(\"Calling validateUserOp from ENTRY_POINT...\");\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 validationData = wallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n\n        console2.log(\"validateUserOp returned validationData :\", validationData);\n        console2.log(\"PASS: multiVault.getAtomWarden() was called during the validation phase\");\n        console2.log(\"      => violates ERC-7562; compliant bundlers will reject this UserOp\");\n    }\n```\n\n```\n[PASS] test_unclaimedAtomWalletValidateUserOpCallsMultiVaultExternally() (gas: 657455)\nLogs:\n    [...] \n  AtomWallet address : 0x9E32F5BB8bbcC1e952CA83b4c4c1C62c2883311a\n  isClaimed          : false\n  multiVault address : 0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9\n  ---\n  Calling validateUserOp from ENTRY_POINT...\n  validateUserOp returned validationData : 1\n  PASS: multiVault.getAtomWarden() was called during the validation phase\n        => violates ERC-7562; compliant bundlers will reject this UserOp\n```\n\nThe `vm.expectCall` assertion passes, confirming that `multiVault.getAtomWarden()` is called during `validateUserOp`. Any ERC-7562-compliant bundler performing the equivalent simulation will detect this call and reject the UserOp.",
